NAME
    tcp - exchange one bounded outbound TCP stream chunk

SYNOPSIS
    tcp ADDRESS PORT [TEXT...]

DESCRIPTION
    Connects once to a literal dotted-decimal IPv4 address and nonzero port,
    optionally writes TEXT, reads one bounded response, and closes. The command
    owns one connection, one at-most-1,460-byte unacknowledged segment, and one
    4 KiB receive FIFO. Each operation is bounded and cancellable. DNS, HTTP,
    TLS, inbound listening, raw packets, and general sockets are not provided.
